c------------------------------------------------------------
c This file belongs to a set of benchmarks that was produced by a minimization 
c of visibly pushdown automata [1, 2]. This minimization encodes the existence 
c of an equivalence relation that is suitable for quotienting. The more soft 
c clauses can be set to true, the more pairs of states can be merged. The 
c input automata were produced by applying the interprocedural analysis [3] 
c of the software verifier Ultimate Automizer [4, 5] to C programs from 
c the SV-COMP 2016 [6].
c
c License "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
c
c 2017-05-22, 
c Matthias Heizmann (heizmann@informatik.uni-freiburg.de)
c Christian Schilling (schillic@informatik.uni-freiburg.de)
c
c [1] Matthias Heizmann, Christian Schilling, Daniel Tischner:
c Minimization of Visibly Pushdown Automata Using Partial Max-SAT.
c TACAS (1) 2017: 461-478
c [2] https://ultimate.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/automata_library
c [3] Matthias Heizmann, Jochen Hoenicke, Andreas Podelski:
c Nested interpolants. POPL 2010: 471-482
c [4] Matthias Heizmann, Jochen Hoenicke, Andreas Podelski:
c Software Model Checking for People Who Love Automata.
c CAV 2013: 36-52
c [5] Matthias Heizmann, Yu-Fang Chen, Daniel Dietsch, Marius Greitschus,
c Jochen Hoenicke, Yong Li, Alexander Nutz, Betim Musa, Christian Schilling,
c Tanja Schindler, Andreas Podelski:
c Ultimate Automizer and the Search for Perfect Interpolants - (Competition
c Contribution).
c TACAS (II) 2018: 447-451
c [6] Dirk Beyer: Reliable and Reproducible Competition Results with 
c BenchExec and Witnesses (Report on SV-COMP 2016).
c TACAS 2016: 887-904
